1
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:45,962
‪SPOOKY IN LOVE

2
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:01,728
‪Get off me!

3
00:01:02,604 --> 00:01:05,065
‪-Mr. Ma! Keep still!
‪-Get off me!

4
00:01:05,148 --> 00:01:06,858
‪Go away!

5
00:01:07,567 --> 00:01:08,651
‪You said you weren't afraid!

6
00:01:10,195 --> 00:01:12,322
‪No! No!

7
00:01:12,405 --> 00:01:13,490
‪Go away!

8
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:17,452
‪He's off your back now!

9
00:01:18,036 --> 00:01:20,163
‪He's gone!

10
00:01:20,789 --> 00:01:22,248
‪He's gone!

11
00:01:22,749 --> 00:01:23,583
‪He's gone?

12
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:25,126
‪He's gone?

13
00:01:35,094 --> 00:01:36,179
‪Do you see the kid?

14
00:01:39,307 --> 00:01:41,518
‪Yes. I see him.

15
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:50,485
‪EPISODE 4

16
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:10,839
‪What…

17
00:02:55,925 --> 00:02:57,176
‪I'll call it in.

18
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:58,094
‪Okay.

19
00:03:05,351 --> 00:03:07,312
‪Hey, are you all right?

20
00:03:08,104 --> 00:03:10,106
‪The back… In the back.

21
00:03:10,189 --> 00:03:11,566
‪-The back.
‪-In the back?

22
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:13,735
‪-Look in the back.
‪-Hold on.

23
00:03:27,206 --> 00:03:29,667
‪My boy. He's okay, isn't he?

24
00:03:32,962 --> 00:03:33,796
‪He's…

25
00:03:34,714 --> 00:03:36,174
‪He's okay, isn't he?

26
00:03:46,184 --> 00:03:47,310
‪He's warm.

27
00:03:50,271 --> 00:03:51,272
‪Good.

28
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:54,234
‪That's good.

29
00:04:11,751 --> 00:04:14,545
‪EMERGENCY SERVICES

30
00:04:24,055 --> 00:04:25,014
‪Gang-uk.

31
00:04:47,787 --> 00:04:50,331
‪Oh, no. Hold on.

32
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:52,709
‪-There's someone here!
‪-Help!

33
00:04:52,792 --> 00:04:54,294
‪-In here.
‪-Over here!

34
00:04:54,377 --> 00:04:56,671
‪There's someone here! Over here!

35
00:04:57,213 --> 00:04:58,756
‪-Where are they?
‪-In there.

36
00:05:00,049 --> 00:05:01,551
‪The child is alive!

37
00:05:01,634 --> 00:05:03,928
‪Her breathing is shallow. Get the oxygen!

38
00:05:04,012 --> 00:05:07,932
‪Ju-young, Daddy will make lots of money
‪and buy you plenty of toys.

39
00:05:08,016 --> 00:05:09,684
‪Be good and listen to Grandma, okay?

40
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:11,019
‪-Okay.
‪-Good.

41
00:05:11,936 --> 00:05:15,023
‪-Do you like that toy that much, Da-young?
‪-Yes.

42
00:05:16,774 --> 00:05:18,067
‪Ju-young.

43
00:05:18,151 --> 00:05:20,611
‪You're the big brother,
‪so look after your sister.

44
00:05:44,052 --> 00:05:46,304
‪We found an injured little girl.

45
00:05:46,971 --> 00:05:48,639
‪Yes. We're loading her up.

46
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:52,643
‪-Get that for me.
‪-Careful.

47
00:05:57,982 --> 00:05:58,941
‪All done.

48
00:05:59,776 --> 00:06:00,902
‪Let's go.

49
00:07:13,891 --> 00:07:16,602
‪When did all this start?

50
00:07:25,236 --> 00:07:26,320
‪I was in a yacht accident

51
00:07:27,822 --> 00:07:29,782
‪when I was in university.

52
00:07:31,826 --> 00:07:32,827
<i>‪Yeo-ri!</i>

53
00:07:35,371 --> 00:07:38,249
<i>‪I stopped breathing completely.</i>

54
00:07:43,671 --> 00:07:45,506
<i>‪Then miraculously, I came to.</i>

55
00:07:53,890 --> 00:07:56,100
<i>‪But my friend who fell in with me…</i>

56
00:07:57,852 --> 00:07:58,978
<i>‪didn't make it.</i>

57
00:08:00,271 --> 00:08:01,981
‪We have two different words

58
00:08:02,064 --> 00:08:04,025
‪that mean "grave," depending on the shape.

59
00:08:04,108 --> 00:08:07,987
‪Some have a high, rounded top,
‪which we call "bun."

60
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:11,824
‪If the body is buried underground
‪with a flat top, it's called "myo."

61
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:16,787
‪There are three different kinds
‪of high, rounded grave tops.

62
00:08:16,871 --> 00:08:18,956
‪The most common type is…

63
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:20,833
<i>‪After that,</i>

64
00:08:22,001 --> 00:08:25,254
<i>‪-I kept seeing Ji-hwan, who had died.</i>
‪-Ji-hwan.

65
00:08:29,133 --> 00:08:30,468
‪What's the matter?

66
00:08:34,013 --> 00:08:35,431
<i>‪That's when it began.</i>

67
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:39,352
‪-It's a lovely day.
‪-It is.

68
00:08:39,435 --> 00:08:40,895
‪The weather is amazing.

69
00:08:40,978 --> 00:08:43,564
‪-Did you have something to eat?
‪-No, not yet.

70
00:08:44,857 --> 00:08:48,444
<i>‪Ghosts that others couldn't see</i>
<i>‪appeared in front of me.</i>

71
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:49,779
<i>‪Are you all right?</i>

72
00:08:52,156 --> 00:08:55,076
<i>‪-And anyone whose hands touched mine</i>
‪-Thank you.

73
00:08:56,536 --> 00:08:58,621
<i>‪started seeing them.</i>

74
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:02,917
‪What's that?

75
00:09:09,966 --> 00:09:12,218
‪-She sees ghosts.
‪-She can see stuff.

76
00:09:12,301 --> 00:09:14,387
<i>‪"If you so much as touch Cheon Yeo-ri,</i>

77
00:09:14,887 --> 00:09:16,764
<i>‪ghosts will latch onto you too."</i>

78
00:09:17,431 --> 00:09:20,518
<i>‪"If you stick around her,</i>
<i>‪you'll </i><i>‪be </i><i>‪cursed </i><i>‪too."</i>

79
00:09:21,644 --> 00:09:23,521
<i>‪Rumors like that started to spread.</i>

80
00:09:25,481 --> 00:09:26,649
‪Ever since then,

81
00:09:27,316 --> 00:09:31,195
‪I've been living alone,
‪like a living ghost.

82
00:09:36,117 --> 00:09:38,869
‪I tried to live a decent life though.

83
00:09:39,704 --> 00:09:41,581
‪There's a lot you can do on your own.

84
00:09:43,124 --> 00:09:44,250
‪Once you get used to it,

85
00:09:46,127 --> 00:09:47,378
‪being alone isn't so bad.

86
00:09:50,756 --> 00:09:54,218
‪I suspected you as an accomplice,
‪not knowing about your background.

87
00:09:57,096 --> 00:09:58,139
‪I'm sorry.

88
00:10:00,224 --> 00:10:02,310
‪I got you all wrong too,
‪when we first met.

89
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:05,396
‪What do we do now?

90
00:10:05,896 --> 00:10:07,565
‪More ghosts will come for you.

91
00:10:09,233 --> 00:10:10,443
‪It can't be helped.

92
00:10:12,695 --> 00:10:15,823
‪What happened to the other people
‪you came in contact with?

93
00:10:17,992 --> 00:10:19,452
‪From what I know,

94
00:10:20,369 --> 00:10:23,581
‪I think they saw ghosts for about a month.

95
00:10:24,832 --> 00:10:25,708
‪And after that?

96
00:10:26,250 --> 00:10:27,752
‪After a month,

97
00:10:28,336 --> 00:10:30,713
‪the ghosts will stop coming for you,

98
00:10:30,796 --> 00:10:32,798
‪as long as you stay away from me.

99
00:10:37,053 --> 00:10:39,096
‪I'm sorry for the trouble I caused.

100
00:10:40,431 --> 00:10:43,267
‪Let's stay away from each other
‪as best we can.

101
00:10:44,143 --> 00:10:45,186
‪If you're around me,

102
00:10:46,145 --> 00:10:47,688
‪you might become miserable.

103
00:10:48,522 --> 00:10:49,732
‪Why would you say that?

104
00:10:50,691 --> 00:10:51,609
‪Bye then.

105
00:10:53,861 --> 00:10:54,695
‪Wait.

106
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:07,833
‪This is day one.
‪The start of that one month.

107
00:11:08,501 --> 00:11:09,585
‪But still…

108
00:11:09,669 --> 00:11:10,795
‪I finally understand

109
00:11:11,545 --> 00:11:13,005
‪what you meant

110
00:11:14,090 --> 00:11:15,549
‪in Jeju Island.

111
00:11:16,092 --> 00:11:17,218
<i>‪Thank you.</i>

112
00:11:18,677 --> 00:11:20,513
<i>‪I might be used to how things are,</i>

113
00:11:21,514 --> 00:11:23,599
<i>‪but that doesn't mean I'm not afraid.</i>

114
00:11:27,061 --> 00:11:28,813
‪It must've been so hard to live with.

115
00:12:03,097 --> 00:12:04,140
‪I'm exhausted.

116
00:12:04,890 --> 00:12:06,767
‪Let me rest tonight.

117
00:12:06,851 --> 00:12:08,102
‪I have a lot on my mind.

118
00:12:25,494 --> 00:12:27,037
‪Will he be okay?

119
00:12:30,166 --> 00:12:31,667
‪It'll be really hard at first.

120
00:13:35,981 --> 00:13:36,815
‪Why…

121
00:13:41,195 --> 00:13:43,697
‪-What was that about?
‪-I don't know.

122
00:13:45,824 --> 00:13:46,825
‪What's so funny?

123
00:13:50,079 --> 00:13:50,996
‪Your name.

124
00:14:05,803 --> 00:14:08,347
‪Oh, my heart hurts…

125
00:14:54,184 --> 00:14:55,811
‪CEO CHEON YEO-RI

126
00:14:55,895 --> 00:14:57,354
‪I wasn't aware of this,

127
00:14:58,105 --> 00:14:59,440
‪but apparently this is a thing.

128
00:14:59,523 --> 00:15:01,233
‪PVC STICKER FOR CARS

129
00:15:01,317 --> 00:15:03,319
‪Print some and put them in the kids' zone.

130
00:15:03,402 --> 00:15:04,862
‪Yes, ma'am.

131
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:08,240
‪One more thing.

132
00:15:09,366 --> 00:15:11,577
‪How old is your child now, Ms. Eom?

133
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:13,787
‪-Four years old.
‪-I see.

134
00:15:15,331 --> 00:15:16,373
‪In that case…

135
00:15:24,131 --> 00:15:26,258
‪If your child happens to like

136
00:15:27,134 --> 00:15:28,761
‪toys or dolls…

137
00:15:34,433 --> 00:15:35,434
‪Thank you.

138
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,251
<i>‪Prosecutor Ma Gang-uk?</i>

139
00:16:01,835 --> 00:16:02,670
‪Yes.

140
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:06,256
‪I think they've been in touch
‪ever since he came here to see her.

141
00:16:07,925 --> 00:16:10,844
‪Are you saying they're dating?

142
00:16:10,928 --> 00:16:12,554
‪I can't say for sure.

143
00:16:14,056 --> 00:16:15,057
‪Okay.

144
00:16:27,861 --> 00:16:29,655
‪What's all this?

145
00:16:30,239 --> 00:16:31,240
‪Mr. Ma.

146
00:16:31,991 --> 00:16:33,283
‪I thought you had no religion.

147
00:16:33,367 --> 00:16:34,618
‪I converted to polytheism.

148
00:16:34,702 --> 00:16:36,286
‪-Polytheism?
‪-Yeah.

149
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:38,414
‪Are you trying to integrate all religions?

150
00:16:39,581 --> 00:16:40,833
‪You believe in all this?

151
00:16:40,916 --> 00:16:43,961
‪Who knows which one actually counts?

152
00:16:44,837 --> 00:16:48,340
‪There's bound to be one
‪that'll scare them.

153
00:16:48,424 --> 00:16:51,468
‪Who exactly are you trying to scare?

154
00:16:52,094 --> 00:16:55,806
‪Well, the punks I deal with
‪are a dangerous bunch.

155
00:16:55,889 --> 00:16:59,560
‪You never know when
‪and which deity will come through.

156
00:16:59,643 --> 00:17:02,521
‪You do look like you could use some faith.

157
00:17:03,522 --> 00:17:06,483
‪Why don't you come over this weekend?
‪I'll keep you entertained.

158
00:17:06,567 --> 00:17:08,277
‪Oh, my mom's calling.

159
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:10,779
‪-Hello? Hi, Mom.
‪-You know,

160
00:17:10,863 --> 00:17:12,781
‪that's a completely ridiculous idea.

161
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:14,408
‪It's the weekend.

162
00:17:14,491 --> 00:17:17,661
‪If I were to suddenly go crazy,
‪then maybe I'd visit.

163
00:17:18,787 --> 00:17:19,705
‪You're right.

164
00:17:19,788 --> 00:17:21,498
‪Weekends are precious.

165
00:17:21,582 --> 00:17:24,376
‪Night duty is better than going home.
‪I'll see you in the office.

166
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:26,879
‪I do wonder what you do on weekends.

167
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:28,297
‪What should we do?

168
00:17:28,922 --> 00:17:31,091
‪Do you play video games? Or board games?

169
00:17:31,175 --> 00:17:32,301
‪Not board games.

170
00:17:32,384 --> 00:17:35,262
‪Let's watch a movie.
‪Something really steamy.

171
00:17:35,929 --> 00:17:37,598
‪-I can't wait.
‪-Good.

172
00:17:37,681 --> 00:17:38,640
‪I'm excited.

173
00:17:42,811 --> 00:17:43,854
‪I can't wait.

174
00:17:49,777 --> 00:17:51,737
‪Don't laugh.

175
00:17:51,820 --> 00:17:53,489
‪You call this steamy?

176
00:17:53,572 --> 00:17:55,365
‪It's a darn old movie too.

177
00:17:55,449 --> 00:17:57,326
‪You called me over just to watch this?

178
00:17:57,409 --> 00:18:00,287
‪Come on, I need to build up some courage.

179
00:18:01,163 --> 00:18:02,790
‪Help me out with some moral support.

180
00:18:04,625 --> 00:18:05,667
‪Pil-dong.

181
00:18:07,127 --> 00:18:09,004
‪Why do ghosts appear
‪in girls' high schools?

182
00:18:09,713 --> 00:18:11,632
‪Well, I mean…

183
00:18:13,092 --> 00:18:16,845
‪wouldn't it be ridiculous
‪if they were to haunt boys' schools?

184
00:18:20,015 --> 00:18:23,393
‪Pil-dong, why do ghosts
‪always cling to people's backs?

185
00:18:23,477 --> 00:18:24,520
‪Well…

186
00:18:25,479 --> 00:18:29,817
‪If they were to cling to people
‪from the front like this,

187
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:32,486
‪wouldn't that look ridiculous?

188
00:18:34,404 --> 00:18:37,783
‪Pil-dong, why do ghosts
‪have straight hair?

189
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:40,410
‪Do you think ghosts

190
00:18:41,537 --> 00:18:44,748
‪would get perms
‪to keep the curls bouncy?

191
00:18:44,832 --> 00:18:46,166
‪Wouldn't that look ridiculous?

192
00:18:47,209 --> 00:18:48,168
‪You're right.

193
00:18:48,252 --> 00:18:52,089
‪Could you just think
‪before you ask a question?

194
00:18:56,718 --> 00:18:58,303
‪-Pil-dong.
‪-What?

195
00:18:58,387 --> 00:19:00,681
‪What is it now?
‪You wanted to watch a movie.

196
00:19:00,764 --> 00:19:02,391
‪It's a sunny Saturday afternoon,

197
00:19:02,474 --> 00:19:04,685
‪and the two of us guys
‪are watching a goddamn movie.

198
00:19:04,768 --> 00:19:06,019
‪-I'm leaving.
‪-What?

199
00:19:06,103 --> 00:19:08,021
‪You threatened me
‪with night duty to come here,

200
00:19:08,105 --> 00:19:11,692
‪-but I can't stand being with you.
‪-Pil-dong, it's not like that.

201
00:19:12,317 --> 00:19:14,278
‪He thinks I'm his lackey

202
00:19:14,361 --> 00:19:16,363
‪-since I'm at his beck and call.
‪-Pil-dong.

203
00:19:16,446 --> 00:19:18,657
‪-Wait, I'll buy you tuna sashimi.
‪-I'm not some lackey.

204
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:19,783
‪I'll order it right now.

205
00:19:22,161 --> 00:19:25,289
‪-I want some belly meat.
‪-Of course.

206
00:19:25,372 --> 00:19:27,624
‪-I only eat Pacific bluefin.
‪-Right, of course.

207
00:19:29,001 --> 00:19:30,043
‪Pacific bluefin.

208
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:32,254
‪Belly.

209
00:19:35,215 --> 00:19:36,967
‪Pil-dong, wait for me!

210
00:19:47,144 --> 00:19:48,812
‪It's only been a week.

211
00:19:51,773 --> 00:19:53,358
‪It's almost time.

212
00:19:53,442 --> 00:19:54,276
‪Right.

213
00:19:54,359 --> 00:19:55,444
‪Let's go.

214
00:20:22,221 --> 00:20:24,306
‪PROSECUTOR MA

215
00:20:30,520 --> 00:20:32,981
‪Yeo-ri, please, please pick up.

216
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:34,441
‪Sorry.

217
00:20:35,067 --> 00:20:36,235
‪It's best that you and I

218
00:20:36,985 --> 00:20:39,029
‪don't cross paths,
‪not even over the phone.

219
00:20:41,198 --> 00:20:44,159
<i>‪The call cannot be connected.</i>
<i>‪You will be redirected to voicemail…</i>

220
00:22:11,288 --> 00:22:13,206
‪Ms. Cheon! Yeo-ri!

221
00:22:13,874 --> 00:22:15,625
‪Ms. Cheon! Yeo-ri!

222
00:22:21,048 --> 00:22:21,882
‪What the heck?

223
00:22:23,842 --> 00:22:24,718
<i>‪Who is it?</i>

224
00:22:26,470 --> 00:22:28,513
‪-I'll leave your package out here.
<i>‪-Okay.</i>

225
00:22:32,851 --> 00:22:33,727
‪It's just the delivery man.

226
00:22:43,403 --> 00:22:44,237
‪Yeo-ri.

227
00:22:46,740 --> 00:22:48,867
‪Wait, why is it closing?

228
00:22:51,411 --> 00:22:53,538
‪If someone calls, at least pick up.

229
00:22:53,622 --> 00:22:55,957
‪I have so many things to ask you.

230
00:22:58,502 --> 00:22:59,419
‪Ms. Cheon.

231
00:23:02,214 --> 00:23:03,590
‪Yeo-ri.

232
00:23:03,673 --> 00:23:04,966
‪I'm sorry.

233
00:23:06,009 --> 00:23:07,969
‪I think this is for the best.

234
00:23:08,595 --> 00:23:11,556
‪I came all the way here.
‪Can't we talk inside?

235
00:23:15,602 --> 00:23:16,853
‪It's tough, isn't it?

236
00:23:34,287 --> 00:23:36,123
‪I could barely get through a week.

237
00:23:38,458 --> 00:23:41,044
‪How did you manage to endure it
‪for ten whole years?

238
00:23:45,132 --> 00:23:46,383
‪To tell you the truth,

239
00:23:46,967 --> 00:23:49,302
‪I blamed you at first, and I was furious.

240
00:23:49,970 --> 00:23:51,721
‪So I came here to complain.

241
00:23:53,265 --> 00:23:54,975
‪But seeing you here,

242
00:23:56,309 --> 00:23:58,979
‪I realize how cowardly and pathetic I am.

243
00:24:01,940 --> 00:24:03,108
‪Unlike you,

244
00:24:04,317 --> 00:24:06,153
‪I just have to hold out for a month.

245
00:24:08,905 --> 00:24:11,741
‪Compared to you,
‪my suffering is a drop in the ocean.

246
00:24:17,539 --> 00:24:19,916
‪Sorry for coming all this way
‪and making a fuss.

247
00:24:21,918 --> 00:24:22,919
‪Don't be.

248
00:24:24,504 --> 00:24:26,590
‪I feel bad for you just the same.

249
00:24:27,340 --> 00:24:29,634
‪Don't be.
‪I'll try to get through it on my own.

250
00:24:31,553 --> 00:24:32,596
‪I'm an adult, after all.

251
00:24:34,139 --> 00:24:35,640
‪Much more so than you were back then.

252
00:24:42,189 --> 00:24:43,190
‪Bye then.

253
00:24:49,362 --> 00:24:50,197
‪Wait.

254
00:24:55,619 --> 00:24:56,453
‪How about…

255
00:24:59,831 --> 00:25:01,166
‪we try this?

256
00:25:12,052 --> 00:25:14,262
<i>‪I don't know if it'll help,</i>

257
00:25:15,096 --> 00:25:18,183
<i>‪but I have a few tips of my </i><i>‪own.</i>

258
00:25:19,517 --> 00:25:22,354
<i>‪The ghosts that visit you early on</i>

259
00:25:22,437 --> 00:25:26,107
<i>‪will be the nasty ones</i>
<i>‪that harass and torment others.</i>

260
00:25:28,109 --> 00:25:29,611
<i>‪But don't let it show.</i>

261
00:25:30,654 --> 00:25:34,282
<i>‪Their favorite moment </i><i>‪is</i>
<i>‪when </i><i>‪you </i><i>‪wake </i><i>‪up from sleep paralysis.</i>

262
00:25:34,866 --> 00:25:37,494
<i>‪Do your best to hide that you're scared</i>

263
00:25:37,577 --> 00:25:40,080
<i>‪and try to sleep as if you don't care.</i>

264
00:25:41,748 --> 00:25:44,292
<i>‪Make them see that you're not affected.</i>

265
00:25:46,753 --> 00:25:48,755
‪Why? Is it not working tonight?

266
00:25:48,838 --> 00:25:51,800
‪That's strange.
‪He's not usually like this.

267
00:25:52,509 --> 00:25:55,679
‪I'm sure he saw us though.

268
00:26:07,399 --> 00:26:08,733
<i>‪Have you spoken to them?</i>

269
00:26:11,319 --> 00:26:12,153
‪Good.

270
00:26:12,737 --> 00:26:15,073
‪Avoid talking to them at all costs.

271
00:26:15,740 --> 00:26:19,577
<i>‪Ignore them </i><i>‪and </i><i>‪hang </i><i>‪in </i><i>‪there</i>
<i>‪for as long as you can.</i>

272
00:26:25,792 --> 00:26:26,835
<i>‪Good job.</i>

273
00:26:55,655 --> 00:26:56,656
‪What's wrong?

274
00:26:59,868 --> 00:27:01,286
‪You must be at a crosswalk.

275
00:27:01,369 --> 00:27:03,580
‪What do I do? He's staring at me.

276
00:27:03,663 --> 00:27:05,874
‪Step on the gas as if you don't see him.

277
00:27:05,957 --> 00:27:06,875
‪What?

278
00:27:07,542 --> 00:27:09,169
‪-Do it.
<i>‪-But…</i>

279
00:27:24,809 --> 00:27:27,145
‪The more you know,
‪the more you can handle.

280
00:27:46,331 --> 00:27:47,165
‪I lose.

281
00:27:53,797 --> 00:27:55,924
‪PROSECUTOR MA GANG-UK

282
00:27:56,007 --> 00:27:58,593
‪I'm almost there. It's nearly over.

283
00:28:06,017 --> 00:28:08,561
<i>‪I just have to last one more week.</i>

284
00:28:08,645 --> 00:28:11,272
‪-Oh, right.
<i>‪-What? What is it now?</i>

285
00:28:11,356 --> 00:28:13,525
‪I got distracted and forgot the basics.

286
00:28:15,276 --> 00:28:16,111
‪Sprinkling salt.

287
00:28:22,325 --> 00:28:24,119
‪Hurl it down hard, with force.

288
00:28:38,007 --> 00:28:38,967
‪Garlic.

289
00:28:40,802 --> 00:28:42,762
‪-Hey, Ma.
‪-No, thanks.

290
00:28:42,846 --> 00:28:44,764
‪-Hi.
‪-Sit with us.

291
00:28:44,848 --> 00:28:46,141
‪I have to go through something.

292
00:28:46,224 --> 00:28:47,767
‪-Enjoy yourselves.
‪-What?

293
00:28:47,851 --> 00:28:52,188
<i>‪I hear they dislike food</i>
<i>‪with strong odors or flavors.</i>

294
00:28:53,481 --> 00:28:56,192
<i>‪In that sense, garlic is very effective.</i>

295
00:29:03,658 --> 00:29:05,577
‪He's definitely acting a bit off.

296
00:29:06,411 --> 00:29:07,454
‪He's lost it.

297
00:29:07,537 --> 00:29:10,582
‪He keeps asking me things like,
‪"Why do ghosts always

298
00:29:11,875 --> 00:29:12,959
‪have long, straight hair?"

299
00:29:13,960 --> 00:29:15,837
‪"Why do they cling to one's back?"

300
00:29:16,755 --> 00:29:19,424
‪There must be something about ghosts.

301
00:29:22,093 --> 00:29:23,595
‪Could he be possessed?

302
00:29:25,847 --> 00:29:26,806
‪Look.

303
00:29:26,890 --> 00:29:28,433
‪Look at him stuffing his face
‪with all that garlic.

304
00:29:28,516 --> 00:29:30,435
‪-What's going on?
‪-What's gotten into him?

305
00:29:33,897 --> 00:29:35,899
‪You know, in movies,

306
00:29:35,982 --> 00:29:38,985
‪people who are possessed
‪stuff garlic down, then spit it out.

307
00:29:41,696 --> 00:29:44,240
‪That's Dracula. Vampires do that.

308
00:29:44,324 --> 00:29:46,534
‪-Oh, right.
‪-Korean ghosts hate glutinous rice

309
00:29:46,618 --> 00:29:47,786
‪-and red beans.
‪-Right.

310
00:29:49,537 --> 00:29:52,290
‪-It's the prosecutor general.
‪-I'm disturbing you all.

311
00:29:52,373 --> 00:29:53,958
‪It's fine. Stay seated.

312
00:29:54,042 --> 00:29:55,376
‪Let's eat over there.

313
00:30:08,515 --> 00:30:10,517
‪Which division are you in?

314
00:30:11,059 --> 00:30:12,268
‪Yes, sir. I'm…

315
00:30:14,854 --> 00:30:17,774
‪I'm in the Cold Case Unit.
‪My name is Ma Gang-uk, sir.

316
00:30:17,857 --> 00:30:21,277
‪Oh, the team they decided to revamp?

317
00:30:22,028 --> 00:30:22,946
‪Yes.

318
00:30:24,781 --> 00:30:26,616
‪-So, sir.
‪-Mr. Ma.

319
00:30:26,699 --> 00:30:30,537
‪I appreciate the intention
‪behind revamping the Cold Case Unit.

320
00:30:32,956 --> 00:30:34,290
‪But the recent personnel transfer

321
00:30:35,583 --> 00:30:36,960
‪was influenced by an outside…

322
00:30:48,096 --> 00:30:50,306
‪-I'm so sorry.
‪-Clean him up.

323
00:30:50,390 --> 00:30:51,391
‪I'm sorry, sir.

324
00:30:51,474 --> 00:30:53,643
‪-Sir, let me…
‪-Oh, dear.

325
00:30:54,811 --> 00:30:56,229
‪I'm so sorry, sir. I was…

326
00:31:01,192 --> 00:31:02,652
‪He definitely did spit it out.

327
00:31:02,735 --> 00:31:03,778
‪Oh, gosh.

328
00:31:10,827 --> 00:31:11,953
‪Yeo-ri.

329
00:31:12,036 --> 00:31:14,664
‪Show me your glass and champagne too.

330
00:31:14,747 --> 00:31:15,874
<i>‪What do you mean?</i>

331
00:31:15,957 --> 00:31:17,709
‪It'll be all over by tomorrow night.

332
00:31:17,792 --> 00:31:21,087
‪Let's celebrate with champagne,
‪even if it's over a video call.

333
00:31:24,257 --> 00:31:25,216
‪Give me a moment.

334
00:31:35,101 --> 00:31:37,770
‪It's like we're drinking alone,
‪but not quite.

335
00:31:37,854 --> 00:31:41,524
‪They say you shouldn't
‪pop the champagne too early though.

336
00:31:41,608 --> 00:31:42,901
<i>‪It'll be fine.</i>

337
00:31:42,984 --> 00:31:45,153
‪What could happen in just one day?

338
00:31:46,613 --> 00:31:48,573
‪As long as there aren't too many of them,

339
00:31:48,656 --> 00:31:50,909
‪I'm sure I can manage on my own for a day.

340
00:31:58,416 --> 00:31:59,417
‪Shall we?

341
00:32:03,212 --> 00:32:04,923
‪-Cheers.
‪-Cheers.

342
00:32:17,185 --> 00:32:18,186
‪Yeo-ri.

343
00:32:19,604 --> 00:32:21,314
‪Thank you for everything.

344
00:32:21,940 --> 00:32:23,942
‪I'm glad if I helped beat the fear.

345
00:32:24,025 --> 00:32:26,819
‪You didn't. I was scared the whole time.

346
00:32:26,903 --> 00:32:28,154
‪What?

347
00:32:28,947 --> 00:32:30,281
‪I was scared the whole time.

348
00:32:31,574 --> 00:32:33,660
<i>‪They have no physical form,</i>

349
00:32:33,743 --> 00:32:37,163
‪and they're not human,
‪so how could I not be scared?

350
00:32:38,373 --> 00:32:39,290
‪That's true.

351
00:32:40,416 --> 00:32:41,292
‪The truth is,

352
00:32:42,669 --> 00:32:45,129
‪I feel the same,
‪though I pretend not to be.

353
00:32:45,213 --> 00:32:46,047
<i>‪Right?</i>

354
00:32:46,631 --> 00:32:48,883
‪So I wasn't the only one to be scared.

355
00:32:49,384 --> 00:32:52,512
‪As soon as one ghost leaves,
‪another one appears.

356
00:32:52,595 --> 00:32:55,098
‪And why are there so many different kinds?

357
00:32:56,808 --> 00:32:58,559
<i>‪I was terrified every single time.</i>

358
00:33:00,603 --> 00:33:01,729
‪But I felt reassured…

359
00:33:03,940 --> 00:33:06,234
‪by your voice
‪that helped me through each time.

360
00:33:10,947 --> 00:33:13,157
‪That's how I was able to get through it.

361
00:33:20,206 --> 00:33:22,500
‪I guess that means I protected you, right?

362
00:33:23,835 --> 00:33:24,794
‪That's pretty rewarding.

363
00:33:26,295 --> 00:33:27,505
‪Thank you, Yeo-ri.

364
00:33:29,882 --> 00:33:32,719
<i>‪Oh, and I did some thinking.</i>

365
00:33:33,469 --> 00:33:36,347
‪Wouldn't it be okay
‪to interact virtually like this?

366
00:33:37,348 --> 00:33:41,144
<i>‪We can check on each other sometimes,</i>
<i>‪or ask for help if we need it.</i>

367
00:33:42,103 --> 00:33:45,523
‪People make friends
‪through social media these days,

368
00:33:45,606 --> 00:33:47,483
‪and even travel online
‪without being there.

369
00:33:52,655 --> 00:33:53,531
‪No.

370
00:33:54,699 --> 00:33:56,367
‪It's best if we don't do that.

371
00:34:02,874 --> 00:34:05,376
‪If you just get through one more day,

372
00:34:06,210 --> 00:34:08,921
‪we can both return
‪to our everyday lives, right?

373
00:34:10,465 --> 00:34:11,966
<i>‪Take care of yourself.</i>

374
00:34:12,550 --> 00:34:14,052
‪Even if we meet by chance,

375
00:34:15,928 --> 00:34:16,804
‪let's pretend…

376
00:34:18,306 --> 00:34:19,474
‪to be strangers.

377
00:34:21,851 --> 00:34:22,894
‪Yeo-ri…

378
00:34:24,145 --> 00:34:25,313
‪Bye.

379
00:34:26,939 --> 00:34:27,815
‪CEO CHEON YEO-RI
‪CALL ENDED

380
00:35:11,567 --> 00:35:13,361
‪Wasn't that a bit too harsh?

381
00:35:14,112 --> 00:35:17,907
‪We'll pretend to be strangers
‪even if we meet by chance?

382
00:35:33,756 --> 00:35:35,133
<i>‪Thank you for everything.</i>

383
00:35:35,925 --> 00:35:38,177
‪I was terrified every single time.

384
00:35:38,845 --> 00:35:40,138
‪But I felt reassured

385
00:35:40,721 --> 00:35:42,932
‪by your voice
‪that helped me through each time.

386
00:35:44,725 --> 00:35:46,769
<i>‪That's how I was able to get through it.</i>

387
00:35:56,863 --> 00:35:59,949
‪You said you could manage
‪on your own for a day.

388
00:36:00,032 --> 00:36:01,909
‪What ghost is it this time?

389
00:36:04,745 --> 00:36:05,830
‪CHEON HA-RI

390
00:36:08,833 --> 00:36:10,459
‪Why do you care who I'm talking to?

391
00:36:11,711 --> 00:36:12,712
‪And don't even think of

392
00:36:13,880 --> 00:36:15,798
‪bringing me down with that again.

393
00:36:22,930 --> 00:36:24,557
‪"What ghost is it this time?"

394
00:36:26,392 --> 00:36:28,686
‪She's definitely hiding something.

395
00:36:35,943 --> 00:36:37,820
‪-Min-hwan.
‪-Ha-ri.

396
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:40,781
‪I'm so touched.

397
00:36:40,865 --> 00:36:43,201
‪You offered to treat me,
‪and you actually came.

398
00:36:43,284 --> 00:36:44,118
‪What?

399
00:36:45,411 --> 00:36:48,206
‪Oh, sure. Is there anything you'd like?

400
00:36:48,289 --> 00:36:49,999
‪Whatever you like is fine.

401
00:36:50,082 --> 00:36:51,876
‪You're a gourmand.

402
00:36:54,337 --> 00:36:56,505
‪By the way, is something up with Yeo-ri?

403
00:36:57,465 --> 00:36:58,299
‪What?

404
00:36:58,382 --> 00:37:01,010
‪I called her a few times since I came,
‪but she didn't pick up.

405
00:37:04,138 --> 00:37:06,515
‪If she doesn't pick up,
‪she's putting up a wall.

406
00:37:07,141 --> 00:37:09,060
‪From what my mom told me,

407
00:37:09,143 --> 00:37:12,188
‪she seems to be seeing
‪some prosecutor pretty often.

408
00:37:12,688 --> 00:37:13,689
‪Prosecutor Ma Gang-uk?

409
00:37:14,273 --> 00:37:15,316
‪How do you know his name?

410
00:37:17,401 --> 00:37:18,236
‪Ha-ri.

411
00:37:18,319 --> 00:37:20,071
‪If you care about someone,

412
00:37:20,154 --> 00:37:21,489
‪you naturally learn all about them.

413
00:37:42,426 --> 00:37:43,302
‪PRO GOLFER PARK'S EX JANG FOUND DEAD

414
00:37:43,386 --> 00:37:48,516
‪PARK WANTED AS LIKELY SUSPECT

415
00:37:48,599 --> 00:37:49,600
‪Damn it!

416
00:37:50,268 --> 00:37:52,853
‪So Cheon Yeo-ri reported it,
‪and that's how Ma found out?

417
00:37:52,937 --> 00:37:53,771
‪I'm sure of it.

418
00:37:55,815 --> 00:37:58,859
‪No wonder they both went on
‪about my monumental fall.

419
00:38:00,027 --> 00:38:01,070
‪Seung-jae.

420
00:38:01,570 --> 00:38:02,905
‪What you said before.

421
00:38:03,489 --> 00:38:05,700
‪-Did you mean that?
‪-About what?

422
00:38:05,783 --> 00:38:07,368
‪You swore on your life

423
00:38:07,451 --> 00:38:10,538
‪that you'd help me take over Reina
‪once you get out of here.

424
00:38:11,497 --> 00:38:12,373
‪You bet I did.

425
00:38:14,000 --> 00:38:15,626
‪Then do just one thing for me.

426
00:38:16,294 --> 00:38:19,839
‪Then you won't have to bother
‪swearing on your life

427
00:38:20,631 --> 00:38:22,508
‪for Cheon Yeo-ri
‪to lose my grandma's favor.

428
00:38:23,092 --> 00:38:25,594
‪It'll ruin her chances
‪of becoming a successor too.

429
00:38:26,721 --> 00:38:27,555
‪What do you say?

430
00:38:37,023 --> 00:38:38,149
‪Mr. Ma.

431
00:38:40,318 --> 00:38:42,445
‪What? I'm going to leave on time today.

432
00:38:42,528 --> 00:38:43,654
‪It's not that.

433
00:38:45,698 --> 00:38:46,615
‪It's Park Seung-jae.

434
00:38:48,159 --> 00:38:49,201
‪What about him?

435
00:38:51,704 --> 00:38:54,165
‪Park Seung-jae was granted
‪a motion for detention review?

436
00:38:54,248 --> 00:38:56,292
‪Why do you care?
‪It's not your case anymore.

437
00:38:56,375 --> 00:38:58,002
‪It may not be my case, but still.

438
00:38:58,085 --> 00:39:00,338
‪It makes no sense that a murderer like him
‪is getting released!

439
00:39:00,421 --> 00:39:02,715
‪You think I granted it? The court did!

440
00:39:05,134 --> 00:39:05,968
‪SEOUL CENTRAL DISTRICT PROSECUTORS' OFFICE

441
00:39:06,052 --> 00:39:07,720
‪It was the prosecutor general's order.

442
00:39:08,637 --> 00:39:11,223
‪He has high hopes for the Cold Case Unit.

443
00:39:11,807 --> 00:39:14,060
‪Do a good job and score some points.

444
00:39:14,894 --> 00:39:17,730
‪And be gentle with the door
‪when you come and go.

445
00:39:18,939 --> 00:39:22,318
‪CORRECTIONAL SERVICES
‪ADVANCING ORDER AND HUMAN RIGHTS

446
00:39:22,401 --> 00:39:23,444
‪-Well done.
‪-Good job.

447
00:39:23,527 --> 00:39:25,863
‪Man, I had the worst time in there.

448
00:39:25,946 --> 00:39:27,198
‪Hey, Park Seung-jae.

449
00:39:31,369 --> 00:39:32,328
‪What now?

450
00:39:32,912 --> 00:39:35,706
‪I was released by the law
‪that you love so much.

451
00:39:35,790 --> 00:39:37,416
‪I know your father got you out.

452
00:39:38,167 --> 00:39:39,502
‪It's my luck to have such a father.

453
00:39:39,585 --> 00:39:41,379
‪Yes, I know that too.

454
00:39:41,462 --> 00:39:45,091
‪I also know your father spent millions
‪to make you a golfer,

455
00:39:45,174 --> 00:39:48,260
‪and that you won the first trial
‪thanks to his connections.

456
00:39:48,344 --> 00:39:51,931
‪Man, getting screwed over like that
‪made me fixate on something.

457
00:39:52,556 --> 00:39:54,266
‪What might that be?

458
00:39:54,350 --> 00:39:56,769
‪I got some meaty intel

459
00:39:56,852 --> 00:39:59,397
‪about a reservoir
‪your father's slush fund is buried.

460
00:39:59,480 --> 00:40:00,481
‪Why you…

461
00:40:02,858 --> 00:40:03,901
‪Watch your back.

462
00:40:04,568 --> 00:40:07,571
‪You could get hurt
‪if you go after the wrong person.

463
00:40:07,655 --> 00:40:08,989
‪You watch your own back.

464
00:40:09,073 --> 00:40:11,742
‪I have nothing to lose
‪because my job isn't my whole life.

465
00:40:12,660 --> 00:40:16,664
‪I guess I'd get no joy going after
‪a guy like you, just scraping by.

466
00:40:18,791 --> 00:40:22,753
‪I plan to find a weakness
‪instead of going after you.

467
00:40:23,629 --> 00:40:24,797
‪What are you on about?

468
00:40:25,381 --> 00:40:26,215
‪Cheon Yeo-ri.

469
00:40:29,468 --> 00:40:31,679
‪I just said her name.
‪What's with that look?

470
00:40:31,762 --> 00:40:34,223
‪Why would you bring her up right now?

471
00:40:34,306 --> 00:40:36,392
‪Wouldn't you love to know?

472
00:40:37,852 --> 00:40:38,811
‪Let's get going.

473
00:41:19,018 --> 00:41:21,145
‪CEO CHEON YEO-RI

474
00:41:22,396 --> 00:41:23,856
<i>‪Even if we meet by chance,</i>

475
00:41:24,815 --> 00:41:25,983
<i>‪let's pretend to be strangers.</i>

476
00:41:33,073 --> 00:41:34,074
<i>‪Yes, ma'am.</i>

477
00:41:34,658 --> 00:41:36,702
‪I saw your message. Is something wrong?

478
00:41:36,785 --> 00:41:39,580
‪The Ministry of Foreign Affairs
‪called about the venue selection

479
00:41:39,663 --> 00:41:41,582
‪for the GA21 banquet.

480
00:41:41,665 --> 00:41:43,334
‪The inspection is in two days, right?

481
00:41:43,417 --> 00:41:46,504
<i>‪They asked </i><i>‪if </i><i>‪it </i><i>‪could </i><i>‪be </i><i>‪moved up</i>
<i>‪to tomorrow instead.</i>

482
00:41:47,213 --> 00:41:48,422
<i>‪May I confirm with them?</i>

483
00:41:49,423 --> 00:41:51,592
‪Go ahead. We're fully prepared anyway.

484
00:41:51,675 --> 00:41:53,928
<i>‪-Will do, ma'am.</i>
‪-Bye.

485
00:42:02,728 --> 00:42:04,605
‪PROSECUTOR MA

486
00:43:25,269 --> 00:43:27,104
‪Who are you?

487
00:43:31,900 --> 00:43:34,570
‪Do I look like the Grim Reaper to you?

488
00:43:34,653 --> 00:43:37,323
‪Why are you digging a hole
‪in the middle of the night?

489
00:43:37,406 --> 00:43:39,116
‪I wanted to bury it right away.

490
00:43:39,825 --> 00:43:41,493
‪The clay jar with kimchi I just made.

491
00:43:41,577 --> 00:43:43,412
‪Why bury it outside
‪when I have a fridge for that?

492
00:43:43,912 --> 00:43:47,041
‪Besides, let your goons do the hard work.
‪They look like experts at that.

493
00:43:48,167 --> 00:43:49,585
‪Watch how you talk.

494
00:43:50,210 --> 00:43:51,879
‪I made this for you.

495
00:43:51,962 --> 00:43:53,964
‪I wouldn't let
‪anyone's grimy hands touch it.

496
00:43:55,382 --> 00:43:57,760
‪I'm worried you'll hurt your hips.

497
00:43:58,302 --> 00:43:59,762
‪Let's go inside.

498
00:44:00,346 --> 00:44:01,889
‪Are you worried I'll get hurt?

499
00:44:01,972 --> 00:44:03,807
‪Of course I'm worried.

500
00:44:04,933 --> 00:44:05,893
‪Here you go.

501
00:44:06,810 --> 00:44:09,897
‪No fridge can store food
‪as well as a clay jar.

502
00:44:09,980 --> 00:44:11,815
‪That's true. Plus, your touch works magic.

503
00:44:12,524 --> 00:44:13,525
‪Right?

504
00:44:15,486 --> 00:44:16,820
‪Try this too.

505
00:44:16,904 --> 00:44:19,365
‪-Here.
‪-Oh, thanks.

506
00:44:19,448 --> 00:44:22,201
‪You really weren't in Jeju Island?
‪I swear I saw you.

507
00:44:22,284 --> 00:44:24,703
‪Why do you keep asking
‪when I wasn't there?

508
00:44:25,704 --> 00:44:26,955
‪Remember how

509
00:44:27,039 --> 00:44:29,416
‪-you told me to beware of water?
‪-Yeah.

510
00:44:29,500 --> 00:44:32,252
‪The crazy thing is,
‪I fell into the sea that day.

511
00:44:35,130 --> 00:44:36,632
‪There's no need to be so shocked.

512
00:44:37,216 --> 00:44:39,259
‪I can swim as well as anyone.

513
00:44:39,343 --> 00:44:42,096
‪Don't you know that even
‪the best of people make mistakes?

514
00:44:42,680 --> 00:44:43,514
‪I do know that.

515
00:44:45,516 --> 00:44:47,768
‪So why did you fall into the water?

516
00:44:47,851 --> 00:44:48,852
‪Well…

517
00:44:51,355 --> 00:44:52,648
‪I slipped and lost my footing.

518
00:44:52,731 --> 00:44:53,899
‪I told you to be careful.

519
00:44:55,442 --> 00:44:56,985
‪-I will.
‪-Goodness…

520
00:44:58,028 --> 00:44:59,405
‪-Anyway,
‪-Oh, dear.

521
00:44:59,488 --> 00:45:02,366
‪the Year of the Black Monkey
‪you keep talking about.

522
00:45:02,449 --> 00:45:04,576
‪Did you hear that from a fortune-teller?

523
00:45:04,660 --> 00:45:05,494
‪Why?

524
00:45:06,203 --> 00:45:08,747
‪Are you seeing someone born in that year?

525
00:45:08,831 --> 00:45:11,166
‪Why would you say that?
‪I'm not seeing anyone.

526
00:45:12,209 --> 00:45:14,545
‪-I'm not.
‪-You're not, right?

527
00:45:15,546 --> 00:45:17,381
‪But what's the deal
‪with that specific year?

528
00:45:17,464 --> 00:45:19,842
‪There's nothing wrong
‪with the year itself.

529
00:45:19,925 --> 00:45:22,261
‪The problem is
‪that it's incompatible with you.

530
00:45:23,971 --> 00:45:24,805
‪Remember that.

531
00:45:24,888 --> 00:45:26,890
‪Okay, fine. Eat up.

532
00:45:30,352 --> 00:45:31,770
‪-One more thing.
‪-What?

533
00:45:31,854 --> 00:45:35,858
‪Don't go anywhere tonight.
‪Stay out of harm's way.

534
00:45:37,317 --> 00:45:38,152
‪Okay.

535
00:45:39,403 --> 00:45:42,281
‪You shouldn't cook so much.
‪You said your wrists hurt.

536
00:45:42,364 --> 00:45:44,950
‪-I'll order delivery. It's just as good.
‪-Enough.

537
00:45:45,033 --> 00:45:47,035
‪Delivery, my foot. Just eat.

538
00:46:01,717 --> 00:46:03,552
‪It must be my grandma's energy.

539
00:46:04,386 --> 00:46:05,971
‪I don't see any ghosts.

540
00:46:07,514 --> 00:46:08,891
‪Or is it because it's the last day?

541
00:46:13,854 --> 00:46:15,105
‪Oh, dear.

542
00:46:17,232 --> 00:46:19,401
<i>‪I plan to find a weakness.</i>

543
00:46:20,194 --> 00:46:21,028
‪Cheon Yeo-ri.

544
00:46:21,111 --> 00:46:23,113
‪Why would you bring her up right now?

545
00:46:23,197 --> 00:46:25,991
‪Wouldn't you love to know?

546
00:46:30,537 --> 00:46:32,164
‪CEO CHEON YEO-RI

547
00:46:34,208 --> 00:46:38,003
<i>‪The phone is turned off.</i>
<i>‪You will be redirected to voicemail…</i>

548
00:47:00,567 --> 00:47:01,485
‪Grandma?

549
00:47:03,111 --> 00:47:06,031
‪-That hurts.
‪-I told you not to go anywhere!

550
00:47:06,114 --> 00:47:07,699
‪Why won't you listen?

551
00:47:08,909 --> 00:47:10,118
‪Goodness.

552
00:47:11,245 --> 00:47:12,204
‪Stay right there.

553
00:47:12,913 --> 00:47:13,914
‪Jeez.

554
00:47:17,417 --> 00:47:18,919
‪She's so strong for her age.

555
00:47:19,920 --> 00:47:23,131
‪Does she know something
‪or is it just a hunch?

556
00:47:26,927 --> 00:47:30,138
‪Why did Cheon Yeo-ri
‪turn off her phone anyway?

557
00:47:41,066 --> 00:47:44,236
‪I feel nasty
‪because I only washed my hair earlier.

558
00:47:44,319 --> 00:47:47,531
‪I'll just take a shower
‪and go straight to bed, okay?

559
00:47:49,950 --> 00:47:51,535
‪Don't take too long.

560
00:47:54,454 --> 00:47:56,540
‪-Why you…
‪-Go to bed.

561
00:47:56,623 --> 00:47:58,292
‪Don't you dare go out.

562
00:47:58,375 --> 00:47:59,668
‪I won't.

563
00:48:15,559 --> 00:48:16,643
‪Hi.

564
00:48:19,730 --> 00:48:21,023
‪You're out of your mind.

565
00:48:21,773 --> 00:48:23,358
‪You're only adding to your charges.

566
00:48:23,442 --> 00:48:24,735
‪That's for me to take care of.

567
00:48:26,111 --> 00:48:27,404
‪I heard you ratted me out.

568
00:48:30,407 --> 00:48:31,366
‪Park Seung-jae.

569
00:48:33,035 --> 00:48:35,037
‪That's not called ratting out.

570
00:48:35,621 --> 00:48:36,872
‪It's called reporting a crime.

571
00:48:39,374 --> 00:48:41,543
‪Whatever you call it, you still did it.

572
00:48:45,505 --> 00:48:48,133
‪How did you know where Jang Eun-ju was?

573
00:48:49,885 --> 00:48:51,428
‪You really want to know that badly?

574
00:48:51,511 --> 00:48:52,679
‪Yes, I do.

575
00:48:52,763 --> 00:48:54,556
‪Ha-ri's right, isn't she?

576
00:48:55,390 --> 00:48:56,808
‪You see ghosts, don't you?

577
00:49:29,591 --> 00:49:31,218
‪F**D M*

578
00:49:35,681 --> 00:49:37,391
‪I heard Shaman Baek suppressed it,

579
00:49:38,892 --> 00:49:39,810
‪but it didn't work, did it?

580
00:49:39,893 --> 00:49:43,897
‪Whether I see ghosts or not,
‪how is that worth kidnapping me?

581
00:49:45,232 --> 00:49:46,733
‪It is worth kidnapping you.

582
00:49:47,776 --> 00:49:48,735
‪You see,

583
00:49:49,319 --> 00:49:50,195
‪it was Ha-ri's condition.

584
00:49:52,406 --> 00:49:54,408
‪She put you up to this?

585
00:49:54,491 --> 00:49:58,537
‪She said to bring back proof
‪that you can see ghosts.

586
00:50:00,122 --> 00:50:02,082
‪But that's not going to cut it.

587
00:50:02,749 --> 00:50:04,626
‪I need something more

588
00:50:04,710 --> 00:50:08,380
‪so you taste the monumental fall yourself.

589
00:50:09,131 --> 00:50:12,551
‪From what I heard,
‪there will be a big scandal out soon

590
00:50:12,634 --> 00:50:15,679
‪about a drug party with celebrities
‪and rich heirs and heiresses.

591
00:50:16,430 --> 00:50:18,557
‪I'm going to make sure
‪that your name is on the list.

592
00:50:18,640 --> 00:50:21,768
‪It'll be a little leverage
‪to keep you quiet.

593
00:50:22,811 --> 00:50:23,895
‪You crazy…

594
00:50:23,979 --> 00:50:25,063
‪Here.

595
00:50:37,993 --> 00:50:38,994
‪What's this punk doing?

596
00:51:16,072 --> 00:51:17,866
‪-Are you all right?
‪-Mr. Ma.

597
00:51:23,622 --> 00:51:24,539
‪Get up.

598
00:51:32,255 --> 00:51:33,256
‪Let's go.

599
00:51:34,216 --> 00:51:35,509
‪Get them, damn it!

600
00:51:37,219 --> 00:51:39,805
‪-How did you find me?
‪-Let's get out of here first.

601
00:51:39,888 --> 00:51:40,722
‪Damn it!

602
00:52:38,154 --> 00:52:38,989
‪Shit!

603
00:52:40,615 --> 00:52:41,741
‪Mr. Ma!

604
00:52:44,828 --> 00:52:46,913
‪-Gang-uk.
‪-Mr. Ma.

605
00:52:46,997 --> 00:52:48,331
‪-Oh, no.
‪-Mr. Ma!

606
00:52:48,874 --> 00:52:49,749
‪Are you okay?

607
00:52:49,833 --> 00:52:52,419
‪-Call for help!
‪-Quick, call an ambulance!

608
00:52:52,502 --> 00:52:54,880
‪-Are you all right?
‪-Don't touch him.

609
00:53:01,678 --> 00:53:02,804
‪Careful.

610
00:53:04,222 --> 00:53:06,266
‪-The ambulance!
‪-Did you call for one?

611
00:53:06,349 --> 00:53:07,267
‪Tell them to hurry!

612
00:53:08,852 --> 00:53:11,021
‪-Wake up! There's blood…
‪-Don't move him.

613
00:53:12,230 --> 00:53:14,441
‪Mr. Ma, wake up.

614
00:53:18,278 --> 00:53:19,112
‪Mr. Ma.

615
00:53:20,739 --> 00:53:21,615
‪Mr. Ma!

616
00:53:23,950 --> 00:53:24,784
‪Mr. Ma.

617
00:53:52,938 --> 00:53:56,942
‪He's a traffic accident victim.
‪Found unconscious, BP is 80 over 40.

618
00:53:57,025 --> 00:53:59,194
‪O2 saturation went down to 89,
‪so we put him on oxygen.

619
00:53:59,277 --> 00:54:00,862
‪Mr. Ma! Hurry!

620
00:54:00,946 --> 00:54:01,821
‪Mr. Ma!

621
00:54:04,491 --> 00:54:05,492
‪Please, Mr. Ma.

622
00:54:08,244 --> 00:54:09,079
‪Mr. Ma!

623
00:54:23,259 --> 00:54:24,427
‪-Mr. Ma.
‪-Wait outside.

624
00:54:24,511 --> 00:54:27,138
‪-You can't come in! Stay here!
‪-Mr. Ma!

625
00:54:27,222 --> 00:54:28,723
‪-Okay.
‪-Sir?

626
00:54:28,807 --> 00:54:30,475
‪Do you hear me?

627
00:54:30,558 --> 00:54:32,602
‪Sir. What's your name?

628
00:54:34,312 --> 00:54:35,939
‪-Check for a pulse.
‪-Okay.

629
00:54:38,024 --> 00:54:40,360
‪He's in Ventricular tachycardia.
‪Starting CPR.

630
00:54:40,443 --> 00:54:42,070
‪-Get a defibrillator.
‪-Okay.

631
00:54:43,780 --> 00:54:46,658
‪-What's wrong? Why are they doing that?
‪-Damn it.

632
00:54:46,741 --> 00:54:48,743
‪-What are they doing?
‪-You can't come in.

633
00:54:48,827 --> 00:54:51,788
‪Take good care of him! Please save him!

634
00:54:51,871 --> 00:54:52,956
‪Mr. Ma!

635
00:55:01,881 --> 00:55:02,841
‪Let's change places.

636
00:55:17,814 --> 00:55:19,399
‪Gang-uk!

637
00:55:19,983 --> 00:55:20,984
‪Gang-uk…

638
00:55:26,281 --> 00:55:27,282
‪Gang-uk!

639
00:55:29,617 --> 00:55:30,869
‪Gang-uk…

640
00:55:30,952 --> 00:55:32,037
‪Mr. Ma!

641
00:55:32,996 --> 00:55:33,997
‪Mr. Ma!

642
00:56:27,008 --> 00:56:28,259
‪It's my fault.

643
00:56:30,929 --> 00:56:32,097
‪Because of me…

644
00:56:43,399 --> 00:56:45,193
<i>‪I could barely get through a week.</i>

645
00:56:46,361 --> 00:56:49,322
<i>‪How did you manage to endure it</i>
<i>‪for ten whole years?</i>

646
00:56:52,117 --> 00:56:53,660
<i>‪I'll try to get through it on my own.</i>

647
00:56:54,661 --> 00:56:56,162
‪I'm an adult, after all.

648
00:56:56,246 --> 00:56:57,914
‪Much more so than you were back then.

649
00:57:05,922 --> 00:57:06,923
‪Here.

650
00:57:09,676 --> 00:57:12,720
<i>‪Let's stay away from each other</i>
<i>‪as best we can.</i>

651
00:57:13,221 --> 00:57:16,141
<i>‪If you're around me,</i>
<i>‪you might become miserable.</i>

652
00:57:20,854 --> 00:57:21,771
‪Mr. Ma.

653
00:57:22,647 --> 00:57:26,151
<i>‪I suspected you as an accomplice,</i>
<i>‪not knowing about your background.</i>

654
00:57:26,651 --> 00:57:27,819
<i>‪I'm sorry.</i>

655
00:57:29,195 --> 00:57:31,281
‪It must've been so hard to live with.

656
00:58:27,295 --> 00:58:28,254
‪Mr. Ma?

657
00:58:33,760 --> 00:58:34,928
‪Gang-uk.

658
00:58:37,680 --> 00:58:38,806
‪Oh, no…

659
00:58:41,518 --> 00:58:42,810
‪Because of me,

660
00:58:44,521 --> 00:58:47,065
‪you turned into a ghost already
‪and came to see me?

661
00:58:49,943 --> 00:58:51,069
‪Oh, no…

662
00:58:54,489 --> 00:58:56,032
‪Oh, gosh…

663
01:00:06,769 --> 01:00:09,147
‪SPOOKY IN LOVE

664
01:00:09,230 --> 01:00:11,482
<i>‪Reporters are already</i>
<i>‪swarming </i><i>‪outside Reina.</i>

665
01:00:12,275 --> 01:00:14,402
‪Should there be any
‪speculative articles or photos,

666
01:00:14,485 --> 01:00:17,947
<i>‪we will take strong legal action,</i>
<i>‪so please step back.</i>

667
01:00:18,031 --> 01:00:19,407
<i>‪They're birds of a feather.</i>

668
01:00:19,490 --> 01:00:21,951
<i>‪Are you doing this </i><i>‪because</i>
<i>‪you </i><i>‪really want to marry Min-hwan?</i>

669
01:00:22,035 --> 01:00:22,869
‪Cheon Ha-ri.

670
01:00:22,952 --> 01:00:26,164
<i>‪Director Ok,</i>
<i>‪should we acquire another masterpiece?</i>

671
01:00:26,247 --> 01:00:29,876
<i>‪Yeeon Museum of Art.</i>
<i>‪The director there is pretty influential.</i>

672
01:00:29,959 --> 01:00:31,753
<i>‪Reina Hotel's slush fund allegations?</i>

673
01:00:31,836 --> 01:00:35,590
<i>‪The artworks displayed at the hotel</i>
<i>‪are supplied by Gallery Cheon, right?</i>

674
01:00:35,673 --> 01:00:37,550
<i>‪How much do you know </i><i>‪about </i><i>‪Yeo-ri?</i>

675
01:00:37,634 --> 01:00:39,093
<i>‪Don't you want to know?</i>

676
01:00:39,177 --> 01:00:40,887
‪Some rumors started
‪after the engagement fell through.

677
01:00:40,970 --> 01:00:41,888
‪Who's there?

678
01:00:41,971 --> 01:00:44,265
‪A bastard like him
‪doesn't deserve to be human.

679
01:00:45,266 --> 01:00:47,644
<i>‪Who are you? Who the hell are you?</i>

680
01:00:47,727 --> 01:00:49,687
<i>‪-Let go.</i>
<i>‪-Damn it.</i>

681
01:00:49,771 --> 01:00:52,523
<i>‪I'll make you regret this.</i>

682
01:00:52,607 --> 01:00:56,569
‪Subtitle translation by: Jennifer Jean Lim
